-- title:
--   Two Igusa branches in the geometric special fibre of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$ and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity; let $K\subseteq L((q))$ be the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$; let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with the tower, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent image the coefficientwise image of $jq=q^{-1}\cdot jNumQ$. Let $\Omega_0$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra of characteristic $p$ and $w$ an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $\Omega_0$, that is, a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral $q$-expansion over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose reduction coefficient is nonzero over $\Omega_0$. Write $\bar X$ for the pullback of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258) (the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ of the scheme glued from the two charts $\operatorname{chartAlg}\,A\,K\,\{j\}$ and $\operatorname{chartAlg}\,A\,K\,\{j^{-1}\}$) along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $A\to\Omega_0$. The assertion is that there are two curve models $M_1,M_2$ over $\Omega_0$ of the Igusa function field $\operatorname{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\,\Omega_0\,M\,w$ — each a datum consisting of an integral scheme $C$, a proper morphism $C\to\operatorname{Spec}\Omega_0$ smooth of relative dimension $1$, an isomorphism of that field with the function field of $C$ over the base, a bijection from the closed points of $C$ onto the places of the field over $\Omega_0$ identifying stalks with valuation rings, and the property that each finite set of points lies in an affine open — together with morphisms $\nu_i\colon M_i.C\to\bar X$ over $\Omega_0$ (that is, $\nu_i$ followed by the second projection is $M_i.\mathrm{toBase}$) such that the ranges of the two underlying maps cover $\bar X$, their intersection is finite, each $\nu_i$ induces an isomorphism of stalks at the generic point of $M_i.C$, and a point $z$ of $\bar X$ lies in both ranges if and only if, in the stalk of the two-chart model at the image of $z$ under the first projection, the ideal generated by the germ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure map fails to have a subsingleton set of minimal primes, i.e. has at least two minimal primes.
--
--   This is the statement that the geometric special fibre at $p$ of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$ is covered by two branches, each birational (via an isomorphism on generic stalks) to a smooth proper model of the Igusa function field of level $M$, the two branches meeting exactly in the finitely many points where the uniformiser has more than one minimal prime in the local ring — classically the two Igusa components of $X_1(Mp)\otimes\overline{\mathbb{F}}_p$, one through $j$ and the other through its Frobenius twist. It makes no smoothness or normality claim about the fibre itself, and is shaped so as to feed the two-branch genus (Euler characteristic) inequality used for the model of $X_1(Mp)$.
